// Official UPSC CDS/NDA/AFCAT Detailed Syllabus Context Map
window.OFFICIAL_SYLLABUS_DATA = {
  "trig-identities": "1. Sub-topics: Trigonometric ratios of angles up to 360°, sum and difference formulae, multiple and sub-multiple angles, trigonometric identities, height and distance problems. 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Sine/Cosine rules, projection formulae, values of standard angles, and application of identities in simplification.",
  "inverse-trig": "1. Sub-topics: Definition, range, domain, principal value branches, graphs of inverse trigonometric functions, properties of inverse functions. 2. Standard: Class 12th level. 3. Exams: NDA. 4. Key Concepts: Principal value calculations, conversion between inverse functions, and solving inverse trigonometric equations.",
  "quadratic-eq": "1. Sub-topics: Roots of quadratic equations, relation between roots and coefficients, nature of roots, formation of equations, quadratic inequalities. 2. Standard: Class 11th level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS. 4. Key Concepts: Discriminant analysis, sum and product of roots, and graphical representation of parabolas.",
  "complex-numbers": "1. Sub-topics: Algebra of complex numbers, modulus and argument, conjugate, polar representation, triangle inequality, cube roots of unity, De Moivre’s Theorem. 2. Standard: Class 11th level. 3. Exams: NDA. 4. Key Concepts: Euler’s form, properties of arguments, and geometric interpretation in the Argand plane.",
  "straight-lines": "1. Sub-topics: Distance formula, section formula, area of triangle, locus, slope of a line, various forms of equations of a line, distance between two lines, angle between two lines. 2. Standard: Class 11th level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS. 4. Key Concepts: Intercept form, normal form, perpendicular distance from a point to a line, and concurrency of lines.",
  "central-tendency": "1. Sub-topics: Mean, median, mode, grouped and ungrouped data, frequency distribution, cumulative frequency, ogives. 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Empirical relationship between mean, median, and mode, and calculation of averages for large datasets.",
  "data-interpretation": "1. Sub-topics: Analysis of tables, bar charts, pie charts, and histograms. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Percentage change, ratio analysis, and extraction of specific data points from visual representations.",
  "limits-continuity": "1. Sub-topics: Concept of limits, standard limits, L'Hopital's rule, continuity of a function at a point, types of discontinuities. 2. Standard: Class 12th level. 3. Exams: NDA. 4. Key Concepts: Evaluation of indeterminate forms (0/0, ∞/∞) and conditions for continuity.",
  "differentiation": "1. Sub-topics: Derivative as a rate of change, derivatives of sum, product, quotient, chain rule, derivatives of trigonometric, inverse, exponential, and logarithmic functions. 2. Standard: Class 12th level. 3. Exams: NDA. 4. Key Concepts: Second-order derivatives, geometric interpretation (tangents and normals), and maxima/minima.",
  "integration": "1. Sub-topics: Integration as inverse of differentiation, integration by substitution, integration by parts, partial fractions, definite integrals, area under curves. 2. Standard: Class 12th level. 3. Exams: NDA. 4. Key Concepts: Properties of definite integrals, standard integral forms, and calculation of bounded areas.",
  "syl-matrices": "1. Sub-topics: Types of matrices, operations on matrices, determinant of a square matrix, adjoint and inverse of a matrix, solution of linear equations using Cramer's rule or matrix method. 2. Standard: Class 12th level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS. 4. Key Concepts: Singular/non-singular matrices, properties of determinants, and rank of a matrix.",
  "syl-probability": "1. Sub-topics: Random experiments, sample space, events, mutually exclusive and exhaustive events, classical definition of probability, conditional probability, Bayes' Theorem, independent events. 2. Standard: Class 12th level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS. 4. Key Concepts: Addition and multiplication theorems, and application of Bayes' theorem in real-world scenarios.",
  "lines-angles-triangles": "1. Sub-topics: Parallel lines, transversal, properties of triangles, congruence and similarity, centers of a triangle (centroid, incenter, circumcenter, orthocenter). 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Angle sum property, exterior angle theorem, and properties of special triangles.",
  "circles-polygons": "1. Sub-topics: Tangents, secants, chords, angles subtended by arcs, cyclic quadrilaterals, properties of regular polygons. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Power of a point, alternate segment theorem, and interior/exterior angle sums of polygons.",
  "area-perimeter": "1. Sub-topics: Area and perimeter of triangles, quadrilaterals, circles, sectors, and segments. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Heron's formula, area of composite figures, and relationship between radius and circumference.",
  "surface-area-volume": "1. Sub-topics: Surface area and volume of cubes, cuboids, cylinders, cones, spheres, and hemispheres. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Frustum of a cone, conversion of solids, and volume of hollow objects.",
  "percentages-profit-loss": "1. Sub-topics: Percentage calculations, profit, loss, discount, marked price, successive discounts. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Profit/loss percentage on cost price vs. selling price, and effective percentage change.",
  "ratios-averages": "1. Sub-topics: Ratio and proportion, variation, partnership, weighted averages, mixture and alligation. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Mean proportional, cross-multiplication method, and solving mixture problems.",
  "time-distance": "1. Sub-topics: Relative speed, trains, boats and streams, work and time, pipes and cisterns. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Speed-time-distance relationship, man-days formula, and upstream/downstream speed calculations.",
  "syl-numerical-speed": "1. Sub-topics: Basic speed, time, and distance calculations, average speed, conversion of units. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Unit conversion (km/hr to m/s) and basic motion problems.",
  "syl-numerical-ratios": "1. Sub-topics: Basic ratio, proportion, and percentage calculations for numerical aptitude. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exams: AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Fraction to percentage conversion and basic proportional reasoning.",
  "parts-of-speech": "Sub-topics: Nouns (types, cases, gender), Pronouns (personal, relative, reflexive), Adjectives (degrees of comparison), Verbs (transitive/intransitive, finite/non-finite), Adverbs, Prepositions (fixed prepositions), Conjunctions (correlative, coordinating, subordinating), Interjections. Standard: Class 10th-12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Identification of parts of speech in context, usage of gerunds/participles, and correct prepositional usage.",
  "tenses-complete": "Sub-topics: Simple, Continuous, Perfect, and Perfect Continuous forms; Sequence of Tenses; Conditional sentences (Type 0, 1, 2, 3). Standard: Class 10th-12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Time-tense consistency, usage of 'since' vs 'for', and conditional clauses (If-clauses).",
  "subject-verb-agreement": "Sub-topics: Proximity rule, collective nouns, indefinite pronouns, compound subjects, inverted sentence structures. Standard: Class 10th-12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Agreement with 'each', 'every', 'either/or', 'neither/nor', and phrases like 'as well as' or 'along with'.",
  "sentence-structure": "Sub-topics: Clauses (Independent/Dependent), Phrases, Parallelism (grammatical balance in lists/comparisons), Sentence fragments, Run-on sentences. Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Maintaining consistency in verb forms and structural symmetry in complex sentences.",
  "voice-conversion": "Sub-topics: Active to Passive transformation, Passive to Active, Imperative sentences, Interrogative sentences, Modal verbs in passive voice. Standard: Class 10th-12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Tense retention during conversion, handling 'by' agent, and passive voice for intransitive verbs.",
  "narration-speech": "Sub-topics: Direct to Indirect speech, reporting verbs, changes in pronouns, tenses, and time/place indicators. Standard: Class 10th-12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Conversion of interrogative, imperative, and exclamatory sentences; handling universal truths.",
  "modifiers": "Sub-topics: Misplaced modifiers, Dangling modifiers, Squinting modifiers. Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: CDS. Key Concepts: Ensuring the modifier is placed immediately next to the word it describes to avoid ambiguity.",
  "punctuation-basics": "Sub-topics: Use of commas, semicolons, colons, apostrophes, and quotation marks. Standard: Class 10th level. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Correcting run-on sentences and clarifying meaning through punctuation.",
  "transformation-sentences": "Sub-topics: Interchanging degrees of comparison, Affirmative to Negative, Assertive to Interrogative, Simple to Complex/Compound. Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: CDS. Key Concepts: Retaining the original meaning while changing the grammatical structure.",
  "synonyms-antonyms-detailed": "Sub-topics: Root words, prefixes, suffixes, contextual vocabulary, nuances of meaning. Standard: Graduation level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: High-frequency words from editorial sections of newspapers, archaic vs modern usage.",
  "one-word-substitution": "Sub-topics: Government types, phobias, manias, professions, scientific terms, literary terms. Standard: Graduation level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Memorizing standard lists of collective nouns and specific terminology for groups/people.",
  "idioms-phrases": "Sub-topics: Animal idioms, color idioms, body part idioms, legal/business phrases. Standard: Graduation level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Understanding figurative meaning vs literal meaning, common usage in military/formal contexts.",
  "phrasal-verbs": "Sub-topics: Verb + Preposition/Adverb combinations, separable vs inseparable phrasal verbs. Standard: Graduation level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Distinguishing between similar phrasal verbs (e.g., 'look after' vs 'look for').",
  "reading-comprehension": "Sub-topics: Inference-based questions, main idea identification, tone of the passage, vocabulary in context. Standard: Graduation level. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Speed reading, identifying logical flow, and distinguishing between facts and opinions.",
  "error-detection": "Sub-topics: Application of all grammar rules (parts of speech, tenses, etc.) in a single sentence. Standard: Class 12th-Graduation level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Identifying subtle errors in syntax, morphology, and usage.",
  "sentence-improvement": "Sub-topics: Replacing underlined segments with grammatically correct alternatives. Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS. Key Concepts: Conciseness, clarity, and grammatical precision.",
  "ordering-rearrangement": "Sub-topics: Para-jumbles (Sentence rearrangement), Word rearrangement. Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS. Key Concepts: Identifying opening/closing sentences, logical connectors, and pronoun antecedents.",
  "fill-blanks-cloze": "Sub-topics: Contextual vocabulary, prepositional usage, conjunctions, and logical flow. Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Understanding the tone of the paragraph to select the most appropriate word.",
  "preamble": "Sub-topics: Philosophy of the Constitution, 42nd Amendment (Socialist, Secular, Integrity), Key terms (Sovereign, Democratic, Republic, Justice, Liberty, Equality, Fraternity), Sources of the Constitution (Government of India Act 1935, UK, USA, Ireland, Canada, etc.). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Nature of the Indian State, Objectives of the Constitution, Kesavananda Bharati Case (Preamble as part of the Constitution).",
  "schedules": "Sub-topics: All 12 Schedules of the Constitution, specifically 4th (Rajya Sabha seats), 8th (Languages), 10th (Anti-defection), and 11th/12th (Panchayats/Municipalities). Standard: Class 10th. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Allocation of powers, official languages, and disqualification grounds.",
  "fundamental-rights": "Sub-topics: Articles 12-35, Right to Equality (14-18), Freedom (19-22), Against Exploitation (23-24), Religion (25-28), Cultural & Educational (29-30), Constitutional Remedies (Art 32 - Writs). Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Writs (Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, etc.), Doctrine of Severability, Waiver of Rights.",
  "dpsp": "Sub-topics: Articles 36-51 (Directive Principles), Classification (Socialist, Gandhian, Liberal-Intellectual), Fundamental Duties (Art 51A, 42nd Amendment, Swaran Singh Committee). Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Conflict between FR and DPSP, Minerva Mills Case, Enforcement vs. Non-justiciability.",
  "citizenship": "Sub-topics: Articles 5-11, Citizenship Act 1955, Modes of acquisition (Birth, Descent, Registration, Naturalization, Incorporation), Termination of citizenship, OCI/PIO status. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS/AFCAT. Key Concepts: Dual citizenship (not allowed), Parliamentary power to regulate citizenship.",
  "president": "Sub-topics: Articles 52-62, Election process (Electoral College), Impeachment (Art 61), Veto powers (Absolute, Suspensive, Pocket), Ordinance making power (Art 123), Pardoning power (Art 72). Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Discretionary powers, relationship with Council of Ministers.",
  "parliament": "Sub-topics: Articles 79-122, Lok Sabha vs Rajya Sabha, Legislative procedure (Ordinary, Money, Financial, Constitutional Amendment bills), Parliamentary committees (PAC, Estimates, COPU), Sessions, Quorum, Question Hour, Zero Hour. Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Money Bill vs Finance Bill, Anti-defection law, Parliamentary privileges.",
  "goverment-executives": "Sub-topics: PM (Art 74-75), Council of Ministers, Attorney General (Art 76), Governor (Art 153-162), CM and State Council of Ministers, Advocate General. Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Collective responsibility, individual responsibility, Governor's discretionary powers.",
  "judiciary": "Sub-topics: Supreme Court (Art 124-147), High Courts (Art 214-231), Jurisdiction (Original, Appellate, Advisory, Writ), Judicial Review, Judicial Activism, Appointment of Judges (Collegium System). Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Independence of Judiciary, PIL, Contempt of Court.",
  "panchayati-raj": "Sub-topics: 73rd and 74th Constitutional Amendment Acts, Three-tier structure, Gram Sabha, State Election Commission, Finance Commission, Municipalities. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Devolution of powers, 11th and 12th Schedules.",
  "amendments-parts": "Sub-topics: Procedure for Amendment (Art 368), Types of majorities (Simple, Special, Special + Ratification), Important amendments (1st, 42nd, 44th, 61st, 86th, 91st, 101st, 103rd). Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Basic Structure Doctrine.",
  "important-articles": "Sub-topics: High-yield articles (Art 32, 44, 108, 110, 123, 143, 249, 262, 263, 280, 312, 324, 352, 356, 360, 368). Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Quick recall of constitutional provisions for rapid revision.",
  "positions-tenures": "Sub-topics: Eligibility criteria, term of office, removal process for President, VP, PM, Governor, CAG, Election Commissioners, UPSC Chairman, Judges. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Age limits, oath of office, and constitutional safeguards.",
  "constitutional-bodies": "Sub-topics: Election Commission (Art 324), UPSC/SPSC, Finance Commission (Art 280), CAG (Art 148), National Commission for SC/ST/OBC, Special Officer for Linguistic Minorities. Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Independence, functions, and reporting mechanisms.",
  "governance-emergency": "Sub-topics: National Emergency (Art 352), President's Rule (Art 356), Financial Emergency (Art 360), Impact on Federalism and Fundamental Rights. Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: 44th Amendment changes, Parliamentary approval timelines.",
  "polity-federal-structure": "Sub-topics: Legislative, Administrative, and Financial relations, Seventh Schedule (Union, State, Concurrent lists), Inter-State Council (Art 263), Zonal Councils. Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Doctrine of Pith and Substance, Residuary powers.",
  "polity-rpa": "Sub-topics: Representation of People Act 1950 & 1951, Qualifications/Disqualifications of MPs/MLAs, Election Commission powers, Model Code of Conduct, Anti-defection law (10th Schedule). Standard: Graduation. Exams: All. Key Concepts: Electoral reforms, delimitation, and disqualification grounds.",
  "what-is-history": "Sub-topics: Definition of history, historiography, importance of chronology, objectivity vs. subjectivity. Standard: Class 10th-12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Primary vs. Secondary sources, periodization (Ancient, Medieval, Modern), significance of historical inquiry.",
  "sources-indian-history": "Sub-topics: Archaeological sources (inscriptions, coins, monuments), Literary sources (Vedic, Buddhist, Jain, Sangam literature, foreign accounts like Megasthenes, Fa-Hien, Hiuen Tsang). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Epigraphy, Numismatics, Paleography, accounts of travelers.",
  "dating-systems": "Sub-topics: BC/AD, BCE/CE, Carbon dating (C-14), stratigraphy, dendrochronology. Standard: Class 10th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Radiocarbon dating, relative vs. absolute dating.",
  "stone-age": "Sub-topics: Paleolithic (Lower, Middle, Upper), Mesolithic (microliths), Neolithic (Neolithic revolution). Standard: Class 10th-12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Domestication of animals, transition to agriculture, tool technology.",
  "chalcolithic-age": "Sub-topics: Copper-Stone age, Ahar-Banas culture, Jorwe culture, burial practices. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS. Key Concepts: Metal usage, rural settlements, painted pottery.",
  "rock-art": "Sub-topics: Bhimbetka caves, themes of hunting and gathering, evolution of artistic expression. Standard: Class 10th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Prehistoric aesthetics, cave paintings.",
  "indus-valley-civilization": "Sub-topics: Harappa, Mohenjo-Daro, Lothal, Dholavira, town planning, drainage, trade, seals, decline theories. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Urbanization, trade links with Mesopotamia, script (undeciphered).",
  "vedic-age": "Sub-topics: Early Vedic (Rig Vedic) vs. Later Vedic, social structure (Varna), polity (Sabha/Samiti), religion (Indra, Agni, Varuna). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Vedic literature (Vedas, Upanishads), transition from pastoral to agrarian society.",
  "mahajanapadas": "Sub-topics: 16 Mahajanapadas, rise of Magadha, Haryanka, Shishunaga, Nanda dynasties. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Second urbanization, rise of monarchies and republics (Gana-Sanghas).",
  "magadha-expansion": "Sub-topics: Strategic location, iron resources, military innovations (chariots, elephants). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Bimbisara, Ajatashatru, Nanda hegemony.",
  "buddhism-jainism": "Sub-topics: Life of Buddha/Mahavira, core teachings (Four Noble Truths, Eightfold Path, Triratna), councils, sects (Hinayana/Mahayana, Digambara/Shvetambara). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Ahimsa, Nirvana, Sangha.",
  "mauryan-period": "Sub-topics: Chandragupta Maurya, Ashoka’s Dhamma, Edicts, administration, economy, society. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Centralized administration, Kautilya’s Arthashastra, Megasthenes’ Indica.",
  "post-mauryan-india": "Sub-topics: Shungas, Kanvas, Indo-Greeks, Shakas, Parthians, Kushanas (Kanishka), Satavahanas. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Silk route, Gandhara and Mathura art schools.",
  "gupta-period": "Sub-topics: Golden Age, Samudragupta, Chandragupta II, administration, land grants, science and literature (Kalidasa, Aryabhata). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Decentralization, temple architecture, Puranic Hinduism.",
  "south-indian-kingdoms": "Sub-topics: Sangam Age, Cholas, Cheras, Pandyas, Pallavas, Chalukyas, Rashtrakutas. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Maritime trade, temple architecture (Dravidian style), local self-government.",
  "ancient-indian-culture": "Sub-topics: Philosophy (6 schools), education (Nalanda, Taxila), science, medicine (Charaka, Sushruta). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Cultural synthesis, intellectual achievements.",
  "early-medieval-india": "Sub-topics: Tripartite struggle (Palas, Pratiharas, Rashtrakutas), Rajput states, Arab invasion (Muhammad bin Qasim). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Feudalism, regional kingdoms.",
  "delhi-sultanate": "Sub-topics: Slave, Khilji, Tughlaq, Sayyid, Lodi dynasties, administration, Iqta system. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Alauddin Khilji’s reforms, Muhammad bin Tughlaq’s experiments.",
  "vijayanagara-empire": "Sub-topics: Sangama, Saluva, Tuluva, Aravidu dynasties, Krishnadevaraya, Hampi, administration. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Nayaka system, foreign travelers (Paes, Nuniz).",
  "bahmani-deccan-sultanates": "Sub-topics: Bahmani kingdom, disintegration into five sultanates (Bijapur, Golconda, etc.). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Cultural synthesis, architecture.",
  "mughal-empire": "Sub-topics: Babur to Aurangzeb, administration (Mansabdari, Jagirdari), art, architecture, decline. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Akbar’s religious policy, Mughal-Rajput relations, revenue systems.",
  "marathas": "Sub-topics: Rise of Shivaji, Peshwa rule, Third Battle of Panipat, administration. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Chauth and Sardeshmukhi, guerrilla warfare.",
  "bhakti-movement": "Sub-topics: Saguna vs. Nirguna, Kabir, Nanak, Mirabai, Tulsidas, impact on society. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Devotionalism, social equality.",
  "sufi-movement": "Sub-topics: Silsilas (Chishti, Suhrawardi), Sufi saints, interaction with Bhakti. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Mysticism, Khanqahs.",
  "sikh-history": "Sub-topics: Ten Gurus, Khalsa Panth, Ranjit Singh, Anglo-Sikh wars. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Evolution of Sikhism, military organization.",
  "european-arrival": "Sub-topics: Portuguese, Dutch, English, French, Carnatic wars, Battle of Plassey, Buxar. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Mercantilism, colonial rivalry.",
  "british-expansion": "Sub-topics: Subsidiary Alliance, Doctrine of Lapse, Anglo-Mysore, Anglo-Maratha, Anglo-Sikh wars. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Imperialism, administrative control.",
  "economic-impact-british": "Sub-topics: Drain of wealth, land revenue systems (Permanent, Ryotwari, Mahalwari), de-industrialization. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Commercialization of agriculture, poverty.",
  "socio-religious-reform": "Sub-topics: Raja Ram Mohan Roy, Brahmo Samaj, Arya Samaj, Jyotiba Phule, Aligarh movement. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Women’s rights, caste reform, rationalism.",
  "revolt-1857": "Sub-topics: Causes, centers, leaders, nature of revolt, aftermath (Government of India Act 1858). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Sepoy mutiny, nationalist perspective.",
  "governor-generals-viceroys": "Sub-topics: Policies of Cornwallis, Wellesley, Dalhousie, Ripon, Curzon, Mountbatten. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Administrative reforms, social legislation.",
  "constitutional-development": "Sub-topics: Regulating Act 1773 to Indian Independence Act 1947, Morley-Minto, Mont-Ford, Government of India Act 1935. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Responsible government, communal representation.",
  "freedom-movement": "Sub-topics: INC formation, Moderates vs. Extremists, Partition of Bengal, Gandhian era (NCM, CDM, Quit India), INA, Partition. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Satyagraha, mass mobilization, revolutionary movement.",
  "post-independence-consolidation": "Sub-topics: Integration of princely states, linguistic reorganization, Nehruvian era. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Nation-building, secularism.",
  "revolutions": "Sub-topics: American, French, Russian, Industrial Revolution. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Liberty, equality, fraternity, socialism.",
  "world-war-i": "Sub-topics: Causes, alliances, Treaty of Versailles, League of Nations. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Imperialism, global impact.",
  "interwar-period": "Sub-topics: Great Depression, rise of Fascism (Italy) and Nazism (Germany). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Totalitarianism.",
  "world-war-ii": "Sub-topics: Causes, Axis vs. Allies, major theaters, UN formation. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Decolonization, global power shift.",
  "cold-war": "Sub-topics: Bipolarity, NATO, Warsaw Pact, Non-Aligned Movement (NAM). Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Proxy wars, nuclear deterrence.",
  "international-institutions": "Sub-topics: UN, IMF, World Bank, WTO, regional blocs. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Global governance.",
  "architecture": "Sub-topics: Temple styles (Nagara, Dravida, Vesara), Indo-Islamic, Colonial. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Structural features, historical evolution.",
  "paintings": "Sub-topics: Cave paintings, Miniature (Mughal, Rajput, Pahari), Modern. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Artistic techniques, patronage.",
  "dance-music": "Sub-topics: Classical dances, Hindustani vs. Carnatic music, folk forms. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Cultural heritage.",
  "literature": "Sub-topics: Vedic, Sanskrit, Pali, Prakrit, Persian, regional literature. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Intellectual history.",
  "religion-festivals": "Sub-topics: Major religions, syncretic traditions, festivals. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Cultural diversity.",
  "heritage-sites": "Sub-topics: UNESCO sites, conservation. Standard: Class 12th. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Preservation.",
  "history-pyq-trends-topic": "Sub-topics: Analysis of weightage (Modern India > Ancient > Medieval), recurring themes (Acts, Reformers, Battles). Standard: Graduation level (Analysis). Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Strategic preparation.",
  "universe-solar-system": "Sub-topics: Origin of the Universe (Big Bang Theory), Solar System components (Sun, Planets, Dwarf Planets, Asteroids, Comets, Meteors), Earth's rotation and revolution, Solstices and Equinoxes, Phases of the Moon, Eclipses (Solar/Lunar). Standard: Class 10th-12th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Kepler’s Laws of Planetary Motion, Orbital velocity, Perihelion/Aphelion, International Date Line, Time Zones.",
  "earth-atmosphere": "Sub-topics: Interior of the Earth (Crust, Mantle, Core), Lithosphere, Composition and Structure of the Atmosphere (Troposphere to Exosphere), Heat Budget of the Earth, Temperature Inversion. Standard: Class 11th NCERT (Fundamentals of Physical Geography). Exams: NDA, CDS. Key Concepts: Seismic waves (P, S, L waves), Lapse rate, Greenhouse effect, Albedo.",
  "climatology-clouds": "Sub-topics: Atmospheric pressure belts, Planetary winds (Trade, Westerlies, Polar), Local winds (Loo, Chinook, Foehn), Cyclones (Tropical vs Temperate), Cloud classification (Cirrus, Stratus, Cumulus), Precipitation types. Standard: Class 11th-12th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Coriolis effect, Jet streams, El Nino/La Nina, Frontogenesis.",
  "geomorphology-rocks": "Sub-topics: Rock cycle (Igneous, Sedimentary, Metamorphic), Plate Tectonics (Convergent, Divergent, Transform boundaries), Volcanism (Intrusive/Extrusive landforms), Earthquakes, Weathering and Erosion. Standard: Class 11th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS. Key Concepts: Continental Drift Theory, Sea-floor spreading, Richter/Mercalli scale, Ring of Fire.",
  "world-geography-mountains": "Sub-topics: Major mountain ranges (Andes, Rockies, Himalayas, Alps), Drainage patterns, World forest biomes (Taiga, Tundra, Tropical Rainforests), Major river systems of the world. Standard: Class 10th-12th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Watersheds, River capture, Orographic rainfall, Biome distribution.",
  "world-geography-straits-deserts": "Sub-topics: Major Straits (Malacca, Hormuz, Gibraltar, Bab-el-Mandeb), Canals (Suez, Panama, Kiel), Hot and Cold Deserts, Major Seas and Gulfs. Standard: Class 10th-12th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Strategic chokepoints, Trade routes, Desertification, Salinity of seas.",
  "syl-geog": "Sub-topics: Himalayan vs Peninsular river systems, Mountain passes (Nathu La, Shipki La, Zoji La), Soil types (Alluvial, Black, Red, Laterite), Soil erosion and conservation. Standard: Class 10th-12th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Drainage basins, Tributaries, Soil profile, Zonal/Azonal soils.",
  "india-forests-wetlands": "Sub-topics: Forest types (Evergreen, Deciduous, Thorn, Mangrove), Wildlife sanctuaries, Ramsar sites in India, Biodiversity hotspots. Standard: Class 10th-12th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS. Key Concepts: Canopy cover, Carbon sequestration, Wetland ecosystem services, Endemic species.",
  "india-resources-farming": "Sub-topics: Mineral distribution (Iron, Coal, Manganese, Petroleum), Cropping patterns (Kharif, Rabi, Zaid), Green Revolution, Irrigation methods. Standard: Class 10th-12th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Multi-cropping, Food security, Mineral belts, Sustainable agriculture.",
  "india-transport-routes": "Sub-topics: National Highways (Golden Quadrilateral, North-South/East-West Corridors), Inland waterways, Major ports, Railway zones. Standard: Class 10th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Logistics connectivity, Port-led development, Strategic border roads.",
  "india-national-parks": "Sub-topics: Location of major National Parks, Biosphere Reserves, and Tiger Reserves on the Indian map. Standard: Class 10th-12th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Protected area network, IUCN status, Flora and fauna mapping.",
  "mapping-borders-capitals": "Sub-topics: India’s international borders (Radcliffe, Durand, McMahon lines), Neighboring countries, State capitals, Union Territories, Coastal states. Standard: Class 9th-10th NCERT. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Geopolitical boundaries, Maritime neighbors, Strategic border management.",
  "geog-industries": "Sub-topics: Iron and Steel plants, Cotton textile industry, IT corridors, Industrial regions of India. Standard: Class 10th-12th NCERT. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Locational factors of industries, Industrial clusters, Economic zones.",
  "geog-geopolitics": "Sub-topics: Indo-Pacific region, Strategic maritime routes, Geopolitical flashpoints (South China Sea, Arctic, Middle East), India's maritime security. Standard: Graduation level (Current Affairs focus). Exams: CDS, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Geostrategy, Soft power, Maritime domain awareness.",
  "geography-pyq-trends-topic": "Sub-topics: Analysis of weightage distribution between Physical, Indian, and World Geography. Standard: UPSC standard. Exams: NDA, CDS. Key Concepts: Repeated themes, Map-based question patterns, Current-affairs-linked geography.",
  "econ-concepts": "1. Sub-topics: Definition of Economics, Micro vs Macroeconomics, Factors of Production (Land, Labour, Capital, Entrepreneurship), Circular Flow of Income, Sectors of Economy (Primary, Secondary, Tertiary, Quaternary). Principles: Law of Demand and Supply, Elasticity, Opportunity Cost. 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th NCERT level. 3. Exams: All (NDA, CDS, AFCAT). 4. Key Terms: GDP, GNP, NNP, Per Capita Income, Market Equilibrium, Mixed Economy.",
  "econ-poverty-employment": "1. Sub-topics: Poverty Estimation (Tendulkar/Rangarajan Committees), Poverty Alleviation Schemes (MGNREGA, PM-KISAN), Types of Unemployment (Structural, Frictional, Disguised, Cyclical), Green Revolution, MSP (Minimum Support Price). 2. Standard: Class 11th Indian Economic Development. 3. Exams: CDS, NDA. 4. Key Terms: BPL, Multidimensional Poverty Index (MPI), Labour Force Participation Rate (LFPR), Food Security Act.",
  "rbi-monetary-policy": "1. Sub-topics: Functions of RBI, Quantitative Tools (Repo Rate, Reverse Repo, CRR, SLR, OMO, MSF), Qualitative Tools (Moral Suasion, Credit Rationing), Inflation (CPI, WPI, Deflation, Stagflation). 2. Standard: Class 12th Macroeconomics. 3. Exams: All (High weightage in CDS). 4. Key Terms: Repo Rate, Liquidity Adjustment Facility (LAF), Monetary Policy Committee (MPC), Base Rate, MCLR.",
  "econ-budget-fiscal": "1. Sub-topics: Components of Budget (Revenue vs Capital), Fiscal Deficit, Revenue Deficit, Primary Deficit, FRBM Act, GST (Structure, Slabs, Council), Direct vs Indirect Taxes. 2. Standard: Class 12th Macroeconomics. 3. Exams: CDS, NDA. 4. Key Terms: Fiscal Consolidation, Tax-to-GDP Ratio, Capital Expenditure, Revenue Receipts, Cess and Surcharge.",
  "econ-trade-bop": "1. Sub-topics: Balance of Trade vs Balance of Payments (Current Account, Capital Account), Exchange Rate Systems (Fixed, Floating, Managed Float), Devaluation vs Depreciation. 2. Standard: Class 12th Macroeconomics. 3. Exams: CDS. 4. Key Terms: Forex Reserves, Current Account Deficit (CAD), Convertibility of Rupee, FDI vs FPI.",
  "econ-reforms": "1. Sub-topics: 1991 LPG Reforms (Liberalization, Privatization, Globalization), NITI Aayog (Structure, Functions, Difference from Planning Commission), Financial Institutions (SEBI, IRDAI, PFRDA). 2. Standard: Class 11th/12th level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Terms: Disinvestment, Ease of Doing Business, Cooperative Federalism, Regulatory Bodies.",
  "five-year-plans": "1. Sub-topics: History of Planning in India, Objectives of Five-Year Plans (1st to 12th), Shift from Planning Commission to NITI Aayog, Major achievements and failures of specific plans. 2. Standard: Class 11th Indian Economic Development. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS. 4. Key Terms: Mahalanobis Model, Rolling Plan, Inclusive Growth, Self-Reliance.",
  "external-sector-institutions": "1. Sub-topics: IMF (Functions, SDRs), World Bank Group (IBRD, IDA), WTO (Principles, Dispute Settlement, TRIPS, TRIMS), Regional Trade Blocs. 2. Standard: Graduation level (General Awareness). 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Terms: Special Drawing Rights (SDR), Most Favoured Nation (MFN), Dumping, Trade Barriers.",
  "reflection-refraction": "Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Sub-topics: Laws of reflection, spherical mirrors (concave/convex), mirror formula, magnification, laws of refraction (Snell's Law), refractive index, total internal reflection (TIR) and its applications (mirage, optical fibers), refraction through prisms, dispersion of light, scattering of light (Tyndall effect, blue sky), human eye defects (myopia, hypermetropia, presbyopia) and their correction. Key concepts: Focal length, power of lens, lens formula, critical angle, dispersion spectrum.",
  "newtons-laws": "Standard: Class 11th level. Exams: NDA, CDS. Sub-topics: Inertia, Newton's First Law, momentum, Newton's Second Law (F=ma), impulse, Newton's Third Law, conservation of linear momentum, friction (static, kinetic, rolling), circular motion, centripetal force. Key concepts: Free body diagrams, recoil of a gun, rocket propulsion, banking of roads.",
  "syl-exercises": "Standard: Class 11th level. Exams: NDA, CDS. Sub-topics: Work-energy theorem, kinetic and potential energy, conservation of mechanical energy, power, universal law of gravitation, acceleration due to gravity (g), variation of g with altitude and depth, Kepler's laws of planetary motion, escape velocity, orbital velocity, weightlessness. Key concepts: Gravitational constant (G), satellite motion, potential energy of a spring.",
  "physics-sound": "Standard: Class 9th to 11th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Sub-topics: Wave motion, longitudinal and transverse waves, characteristics of sound (pitch, loudness, quality), speed of sound in different media, reflection of sound (echo, reverberation), ultrasound, SONAR, human ear structure. Key concepts: Frequency, wavelength, amplitude, time period, Doppler effect basics.",
  "physics-em-waves": "Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS. Sub-topics: Electromagnetic spectrum (Radio waves, Microwaves, Infrared, Visible, UV, X-rays, Gamma rays), properties of EM waves, transverse nature, speed of light in vacuum. Key concepts: Wavelength and frequency order of the spectrum, applications of each wave type in communication and medicine.",
  "physics-heat": "Standard: Class 11th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Sub-topics: Temperature scales (Celsius, Fahrenheit, Kelvin), thermal expansion, calorimetry, specific heat capacity, latent heat, modes of heat transfer (conduction, convection, radiation), Newton's law of cooling, thermodynamics basics (first law, isothermal/adiabatic processes). Key concepts: Triple point of water, greenhouse effect, thermal conductivity.",
  "physics-electricity-magnetism": "Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Sub-topics: Electric charge, Coulomb's law, electric current, Ohm's law, resistance, resistivity, series and parallel combinations, heating effect of current (Joule's law), electric power, magnetic field lines, magnetic effect of current (Oersted's experiment), solenoid, electromagnetic induction (Faraday's laws), AC/DC current, transformers. Key concepts: Fleming's left/right-hand rules, fuse, short-circuiting, earthing.",
  "physics-nuclear-basics": "Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS. Sub-topics: Atomic structure (Rutherford/Bohr models), mass number, atomic number, isotopes, isobars, radioactivity (alpha, beta, gamma decay), nuclear fission, nuclear fusion, chain reactions, nuclear reactors, binding energy. Key concepts: Half-life, mass-energy equivalence (E=mc²), nuclear energy sources.",
  "physics-units-everyday": "Standard: Class 9th to 12th level. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Sub-topics: SI units, fundamental and derived units, dimensional analysis, scalar and vector quantities, distance vs displacement, speed vs velocity, acceleration, everyday applications of physics principles (e.g., why we lean forward in a bus, working of a pressure cooker, capillary action). Key concepts: Significant figures, precision, accuracy, common physical constants.",
  "physics-pyq-trends-topic": "Standard: Analytical. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. Sub-topics: Analysis of weightage distribution across mechanics, optics, and electricity. Identification of recurring conceptual questions vs numerical problems. Strategy for high-yield topics like Optics and Electricity. Key concepts: Understanding the UPSC pattern of shifting focus between conceptual clarity and application-based questions.",
  "acids-bases": "1. Sub-topics: Arrhenius, Bronsted-Lowry, and Lewis concepts of acids and bases; pH scale and its calculation; Universal indicators; Properties of acids and bases; Neutralization reactions; Salts (types, preparation, and properties); Common salts like NaCl, NaHCO3, Na2CO3, bleaching powder, and Plaster of Paris. 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. 3. Exam: All (NDA, CDS, AFCAT). 4. Key Concepts: pH of common substances, amphoteric oxides, water of crystallization, and indicators like phenolphthalein and methyl orange.",
  "syl-numerical": "1. Sub-topics: Periodic Table (trends in atomic size, valency, ionization energy, electronegativity); Chemical Bonding (Ionic, Covalent, and Coordinate bonds); Lewis dot structures; VSEPR theory basics; Hybridization (sp, sp2, sp3); Polarity of molecules. 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. 3. Exam: All (NDA, CDS, AFCAT). 4. Key Concepts: Modern Periodic Law, Mendeleev’s table, octet rule, hydrogen bonding, and metallic bonding.",
  "metals-alloys": "1. Sub-topics: Physical and chemical properties of metals and non-metals; Extraction of metals (metallurgy); Roasting, calcination, and electrolytic refining; Alloys (composition and uses of brass, bronze, solder, stainless steel, amalgam). 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exam: All (NDA, CDS, AFCAT). 4. Key Concepts: Ores of common metals (Iron, Aluminum, Copper), corrosion and its prevention (galvanization, alloying).",
  "reactivity-series": "1. Sub-topics: Reactivity series of metals; Displacement reactions; Redox reactions (oxidation and reduction); Balancing chemical equations; Exothermic and endothermic reactions. 2. Standard: Class 10th level. 3. Exam: All (NDA, CDS, AFCAT). 4. Key Concepts: Displacement of hydrogen from acids, reactivity order (K, Na, Ca, Mg, Al, Zn, Fe, Pb, H, Cu, Hg, Ag, Au).",
  "carbon-compounds": "1. Sub-topics: Catenation and tetravalency; Nomenclature of hydrocarbons (IUPAC); Functional groups (alcohols, aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids); Homologous series; Chemical properties (combustion, oxidation, addition, substitution); Soaps and detergents (micelle formation). 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. 3. Exam: All (NDA, CDS, AFCAT). 4. Key Concepts: Isomerism, ethanol and ethanoic acid properties, saponification, and cleansing action of soap.",
  "chemistry-numericals": "1. Sub-topics: Mole concept; Avogadro’s number; Molar mass; Percentage composition; Empirical and molecular formulas; Concentration terms (Molarity, Molality, Normality, Mass percentage). 2. Standard: Class 11th level. 3. Exam: CDS and NDA (occasionally). 4. Key Concepts: Stoichiometry, limiting reagents, and conversion between mass, volume, and moles.",
  "chemistry-everyday-fertilisers": "1. Sub-topics: Chemistry in food (preservatives, artificial sweeteners); Medicines (antacids, analgesics, antibiotics); Fertilisers (NPK, urea, superphosphates); Fuels (calorific value, coal, petroleum, natural gas, biogas). 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. 3. Exam: All (NDA, CDS, AFCAT). 4. Key Concepts: Octane number, LPG/CNG composition, and classification of fertilizers.",
  "environmental-chemistry": "1. Sub-topics: Atmospheric pollution; Greenhouse effect; Global warming; Acid rain; Ozone layer depletion; Water pollution (BOD, COD); Green chemistry. 2. Standard: Class 11th to 12th level. 3. Exam: CDS and NDA. 4. Key Concepts: Pollutants (CO, SO2, NO2, CFCs), smog (photochemical and classical), and sustainable development.",
  "cell-structure": "1. Sub-topics: Cell theory, Prokaryotic vs Eukaryotic cells, Cell organelles (Mitochondria, Ribosomes, Lysosomes, Golgi apparatus, Endoplasmic Reticulum, Nucleus), Cell membrane structure (Fluid Mosaic Model), Cell division (Mitosis and Meiosis phases). 2. Standard: Class 9th to 10th NCERT level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key concepts: Powerhouse of the cell, Suicide bags, Cell wall composition in plants vs fungi, Chromosome structure, Significance of Meiosis in gamete formation.",
  "human-systems": "1. Sub-topics: Digestive system (enzymes and absorption), Respiratory system (gas exchange), Circulatory system (heart structure, blood components, blood groups), Excretory system (nephron function), Nervous system (neurons, brain parts, reflex arc), Endocrine system (glands and hormones). 2. Standard: Class 10th NCERT level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key concepts: Hemoglobin function, ABO blood grouping, Role of Insulin/Glucagon, Nerve impulse transmission, Kidney filtration mechanism.",
  "diseases": "1. Sub-topics: Classification of diseases (Communicable vs Non-communicable), Pathogens (Bacteria, Viruses, Fungi, Protozoa), Vector-borne diseases (Malaria, Dengue), Deficiency diseases (Vitamins and Minerals). 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th NCERT level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key concepts: Causative agents of TB, Typhoid, AIDS, Malaria; Vitamin deficiency symptoms (Scurvy, Beri-beri, Rickets), Zoonotic diseases.",
  "immunity-vaccines": "1. Sub-topics: Innate vs Adaptive immunity, Antibodies and Antigens, Vaccination principles, Immunization schedules, Antibiotics vs Vaccines. 2. Standard: Class 12th Biology (Health and Disease chapter). 3. Exams: CDS, NDA. 4. Key concepts: Primary and secondary immune response, Active vs Passive immunity, Mechanism of action of vaccines, Herd immunity.",
  "plant-kingdom": "1. Sub-topics: Classification (Thallophyta, Bryophyta, Pteridophyta, Gymnosperms, Angiosperms), Monocots vs Dicots, Plant tissues (Xylem, Phloem, Meristematic). 2. Standard: Class 9th to 11th NCERT level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS. 4. Key concepts: Vascular vs Non-vascular plants, Seed-bearing vs Non-seed-bearing, Photosynthetic pigments, Economic importance of algae.",
  "animal-kingdom": "1. Sub-topics: Phylum classification (Porifera to Chordata), Vertebrate classes (Pisces, Amphibia, Reptilia, Aves, Mammalia), Characteristics of invertebrates. 2. Standard: Class 9th to 11th NCERT level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS. 4. Key concepts: Cold-blooded vs Warm-blooded animals, Excretory organs in different phyla, Symmetry and Coelom, Respiratory organs (Gills, Lungs, Skin).",
  "plant-reproduction": "1. Sub-topics: Parts of a flower, Pollination (Self vs Cross), Fertilization, Seed germination, Plant hormones (Auxins, Gibberellins, Cytokinins, Abscisic acid, Ethylene). 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th NCERT level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS. 4. Key concepts: Role of hormones in growth and ripening, Double fertilization in Angiosperms, Vegetative propagation, Phototropism and Geotropism.",
  "biology-ecology-basics": "1. Sub-topics: Ecosystem components (Biotic/Abiotic), Food chains and Food webs, Trophic levels, Ecological pyramids (Number, Biomass, Energy), Biodiversity and Conservation, Pollution and Global warming. 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th NCERT level. 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key concepts: 10% energy transfer law, Bio-magnification, Greenhouse effect, Ozone depletion, National Parks and Biosphere Reserves.",
  "rank-equivalence": "1. Sub-topics: Hierarchy of Commissioned Officers (Army, Navy, Air Force), Junior Commissioned Officers (JCOs), Non-Commissioned Officers (NCOs), and equivalent civilian ranks in the Ministry of Defence. 2. Standard: General Awareness (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Comparison of ranks from Field Marshal/Admiral of the Fleet/Marshal of the IAF down to Second Lieutenant/Pilot Officer; insignia recognition; order of precedence.",
  "commands": "1. Sub-topics: Geographical distribution of Operational and Functional Commands of the Indian Army, Indian Navy, and Indian Air Force; Headquarters locations; roles of the Integrated Defence Staff (IDS) and Chief of Defence Staff (CDS). 2. Standard: General Awareness (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Command headquarters locations (e.g., Western Air Command, Southern Naval Command), role of the tri-service theatre commands.",
  "defence-organisations-weapons": "1. Sub-topics: Roles of DRDO, HAL, BEL, OFB; Indigenous weapon systems (Tejas, Arjun, INS Vikrant); International defence agreements (e.g., LEMOA, BECA, GSOMIA). 2. Standard: General Awareness (Class 12th level). 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Strategic partnerships, indigenization projects (Make in India), and major procurement deals.",
  "bilateral-exercises": "1. Sub-topics: Names of joint exercises (e.g., Yudh Abhyas, Malabar, Garuda, Varuna, Hand-in-Hand); participating nations; objectives and locations. 2. Standard: General Awareness (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Frequency of exercises, host countries, and specific domains (Naval, Air, or Counter-insurgency).",
  "missiles-systems": "1. Sub-topics: The five missiles of IGMDP (Patna: Prithvi, Agni, Trishul, Nag, Akash); classification by range, propulsion (solid/liquid fuel), and guidance systems (IR, Radar, Laser). 2. Standard: General Science/GK (Class 12th level). 3. Exams: NDA, CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Ballistic vs. Cruise missiles, BrahMos (joint venture), and strategic deterrence capabilities.",
  "syl-verbal-reasoning": "1. Sub-topics: Analogy, Classification, Coding-Decoding, Blood Relations, Direction Sense, Syllogism, Seating Arrangement, Data Sufficiency. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: CDS (OTA), AFCAT, SSB OIR. 4. Key Concepts: Logical deduction, pattern recognition, and speed-based problem solving.",
  "syl-nonverbal-reasoning": "1. Sub-topics: Series completion, Mirror images, Water images, Paper folding/cutting, Embedded figures, Figure matrix. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: CDS (OTA), AFCAT, SSB OIR. 4. Key Concepts: Visual perception, rotation, and symmetry.",
  "syl-afcat-spatial": "1. Sub-topics: Spatial ability, Hidden figures, Rotation of figures, Dot situation, Grouping of identical figures, Analogy of shapes. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, SSB OIR. 4. Key Concepts: Mental rotation, spatial visualization, and complex pattern identification.",
  "ca-schemes": "1. Sub-topics: Ministry-wise flagship schemes (e.g., PM-KISAN, Jal Jeevan Mission, Ayushman Bharat), eligibility criteria, budgetary allocations, and implementation agencies. 2. Standard: Graduation level (Analytical approach required for CDS/AFCAT; factual for NDA). 3. Exams: All (NDA, CDS, AFCAT). 4. Key Concepts: Beneficiary identification, nodal ministries, 'Sabka Saath Sabka Vikas' initiatives, and socio-economic impact metrics.",
  "ca-relations": "1. Sub-topics: Bilateral summits, strategic partnerships (QUAD, BRICS, SCO, G20), border disputes, trade agreements (FTAs), and India's 'Neighbourhood First' policy. 2. Standard: Graduation level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT (High weightage in CDS GS Paper). 4. Key Concepts: Geopolitics, maritime security, diplomatic protocols, and multilateral institutional frameworks.",
  "ca-policies": "1. Sub-topics: National Education Policy (NEP), National Logistics Policy, Defence Acquisition Procedure (DAP), and Environmental/Climate policies. 2. Standard: Graduation level. 3. Exams: All. 4. Key Concepts: Policy objectives, legislative backing, long-term national goals, and inter-ministerial coordination.",
  "ca-summits": "1. Sub-topics: G20, COP (Climate Change), ASEAN, UNGA sessions, and regional security dialogues. 2. Standard: Graduation level. 3. Exams: All. 4. Key Concepts: Host nations, theme/motto of the summit, joint declarations, and India's stance on global issues.",
  "ca-reports": "1. Sub-topics: Global Hunger Index, Ease of Doing Business (historical context), Human Development Index (HDI), and NITI Aayog reports. 2. Standard: Graduation level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Methodology of indices, ranking of India, publishing organizations, and key parameters used for calculation.",
  "ca-judgments": "1. Sub-topics: Basic Structure Doctrine, Right to Privacy, landmark constitutional amendments, and recent SC rulings on civil liberties. 2. Standard: Graduation level (Polity-oriented). 3. Exams: CDS, NDA. 4. Key Concepts: Judicial review, Article 32, Article 226, and the separation of powers.",
  "ca-awards": "1. Sub-topics: Padma Awards, Bharat Ratna, Gallantry Awards (Param Vir Chakra, Shaurya Chakra), and Sports awards (Khel Ratna). 2. Standard: Class 10th to 12th level. 3. Exams: All. 4. Key Concepts: Award categories, selection criteria, and notable recipients in the current year.",
  "ca-economic-measures": "1. Sub-topics: Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) decisions, Union Budget highlights, RBI circulars, and FDI norms. 2. Standard: Graduation level. 3. Exams: CDS, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Repo rate, inflation targeting, fiscal deficit, and capital expenditure.",
  "ca-science-tech-space": "1. Sub-topics: ISRO missions (Chandrayaan, Aditya-L1), DRDO missile systems (Agni, BrahMos), AI developments, and biotechnology breakthroughs. 2. Standard: Class 12th level (Physics/Biology basics). 3. Exams: All. 4. Key Concepts: Launch vehicles, orbit types (LEO/GEO), indigenous defence production, and emerging tech (Quantum/AI).",
  "ca-upsc-master-framework": "1. Sub-topics: Integration of static GK with current events, map-based current affairs, and interdisciplinary analysis of news. 2. Standard: Graduation level. 3. Exams: All. 4. Key Concepts: UPSC's 'Dynamic Static' approach, linking historical events to current geopolitical developments, and analytical reasoning.",
  "env-hotspots": "Sub-topics: Definition and criteria for Biodiversity Hotspots (Myers' criteria), distribution of hotspots in India (Himalayas, Indo-Burma, Western Ghats, Sundaland), Biosphere Reserve zonation (Core, Buffer, Transition), MAB (Man and the Biosphere) programme. Standard: Class 12th Geography/Biology. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Endemism, Keystone species, UNESCO World Network of Biosphere Reserves, ecological niche.",
  "env-conservation": "Sub-topics: Wildlife Protection Act 1972 (Schedules), Project Tiger, Project Elephant, Project Hangul, Crocodile Conservation Project, Vulture Conservation, National Parks vs. Wildlife Sanctuaries vs. Conservation Reserves. Standard: Class 12th level. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: In-situ vs. Ex-situ conservation, Protected Area Network, Community Reserves, legal status of wildlife.",
  "env-species": "Sub-topics: IUCN Red List categories (Extinct to Least Concern), CITES Appendices, CMS (Convention on Migratory Species), Schedule I species of WPA 1972, invasive alien species. Standard: Graduation level (Current Affairs focus). Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Critically Endangered, Flagship species, Umbrella species, indicator species, biological invasion.",
  "env-treaties": "Sub-topics: UNFCCC, Kyoto Protocol, Paris Agreement (NDCs), Montreal Protocol (Ozone), Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD), Nagoya and Cartagena Protocols, COP summits. Standard: Graduation level. Exams: CDS, NDA. Key Concepts: Carbon credits, Common But Differentiated Responsibilities (CBDR), Net Zero targets, Intended Nationally Determined Contributions.",
  "env-laws": "Sub-topics: Environment Protection Act 1986, Air (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act 1981, Water Act 1974, Forest Conservation Act 1980, Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) process, Coastal Regulation Zone (CRZ) notifications. Standard: Graduation level. Exams: CDS. Key Concepts: Statutory bodies (CPCB, SPCB), public hearing in EIA, environmental clearance process.",
  "env-renewable": "Sub-topics: Solar energy (ISA), Wind energy, Biofuels (National Policy on Biofuels), Hydrogen Mission, Geothermal and Tidal energy, Energy efficiency standards (BEE). Standard: Class 10th-12th level. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Photovoltaic cells, grid parity, renewable purchase obligations, energy security.",
  "env-pollution": "Sub-topics: Types of pollutants (Primary/Secondary), Air Quality Index (AQI), E-waste management, Plastic waste management, Solid Waste Management Rules, Clean India Mission (Swachh Bharat Abhiyan), Namami Gange. Standard: Class 10th-12th level. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. Key Concepts: Bioaccumulation, Biomagnification, Eutrophication, particulate matter (PM 2.5/10), carbon footprint.",
  "econ-govt-schemes": "1. Sub-topics: Key welfare schemes and financial inclusion programs in India. Nodal ministries, funding patterns (Centrally Sponsored vs. Central Sector), target groups, eligibility criteria, and budgetary allocations. Flagship schemes: PM Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY), PM MUDRA Yojana, Atal Pension Yojana (APY), PM Jeevan Jyoti Bima Yojana (PMJJBY), PM Suraksha Bima Yojana (PMSBY), PM Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM-KISAN), PM Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY), Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA), PM Awas Yojana (PMAY), PM Ujjwala Yojana (PMUY), PM-PRANAM, PM-Vikas, PM Surya Ghar (Muft Bijli Yojana). 2. Standard: Graduation level (Analytical approach for CDS; factual for NDA). 3. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: Financial Inclusion, Social Security, Social Safety Nets, Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT), Centrally Sponsored vs. Central Sector funding, Ministry jurisdictions (Finance, Agriculture, Rural Development, MoPNG)."
,
  "ca-red-sea-crisis": "1. Sub-topics: Red Sea Crisis, Houthi shipping attacks, Bab-el-Mandeb Strait chokepoint geography, Cape of Good Hope redirection, economic impacts. 2. India's Response: Operation Sankalp, stealth destroyer deployments, anti-piracy, merchant vessel escorts. 3. Coalitions: US-led Operation Prosperity Guardian, EU Operation Aspides. 4. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT.",
  "ca-quad-indopacific": "1. Sub-topics: Geopolitics of Indo-Pacific, First Island Chain, South China Sea claims, Nine-Dash Line, UNCLOS maritime zones. 2. Quad Dialogue: India, USA, Japan, Australia cooperation, IPMDA (Indo-Pacific Maritime Domain Awareness). 3. Exercises: Malabar (Quad), Milan (multilateral), Pitch Black (multilateral). 4. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT.",
  "ca-defense-acquisitions": "1. Sub-topics: Rafale-M fighter jet procurement, integration with INS Vikrant/Vikramaditya (STOBAR). 2. Submarines: Kalvari-class Scorpene expansion at Mazagon Dock (MDL), AIP system, Project-75I. 3. Air Defense: S-400 Triumf capabilities. 4. Agreements: Reciprocal Logistics Pacts (RELOS with Russia, LEMOA with US). 5. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT.",
  "ca-icet-drones": "1. Sub-topics: iCET framework, semiconductor fab, space coordination, INDUS-X. 2. Engine Deal: GE F414 jet engine co-production with HAL, 80 percent technology transfer. 3. Drones: MQ-9B Predator (SeaGuardian/SkyGuardian) UAV procurement (31 units), capabilities, service distribution. 4. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT.",
  "ca-spain-c295": "1. Sub-topics: C-295 tactical transport aircraft procurement, replacement of HS-748 Avro fleet. 2. Manufacture: Airbus and Tata Advanced Systems (TASL) Vadodara assembly line, private sector military aviation. 3. Performance: Payload capacity, STOL parameters for remote Advanced Landing Grounds. 4. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT.",
  "ca-space-nuclear": "1. Sub-topics: Mission Divyastra, Agni-V flight test with MIRV technology, ICBM range and nuclear triad. 2. Manned Space: Gaganyaan spaceflight, HLVM3 rocket, crew parameters, Vyommitra humanoid robot. 3. Space Defense: Mission Shakti (ASAT), Defense Space Agency (DSA). 4. Exams: CDS, NDA, AFCAT.",
  "afcat-r-analogy": "1. Sub-topics: Word Analogy (synonym, antonym, country-capital, tool-worker, young-ones, dwelling), Letter Analogy (positional shift, opposite-letter pairs), Number Analogy (squares, cubes, arithmetic operations), Mixed Analogy (letter-to-number coding). 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, CDS (OTA). 4. Key Concepts: Opposite letter formula (27 - position), forward/backward letter rank, identifying the exact rule before scanning options.",
  "afcat-r-classification": "1. Sub-topics: Word Classification (category membership), Letter Classification (spacing pattern), Number Classification (prime, square, cube, divisibility), Alpha-Numeric Classification. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, CDS (OTA). 4. Key Concepts: Checking all four properties (prime, square, cube, divisibility) before declaring the odd one; verifying spacing gap consistency in letter sets.",
  "afcat-r-series": "1. Sub-topics: Number Series (inserting missing term, finding wrong number), Alphabet Series (letter sequences, alpha-numeric series), Continuous Pattern Series (repetitive letter sequences with blanks). 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, CDS (OTA). 4. Key Concepts: Tracking letter and number components separately; writing out the full repetition pattern before filling blanks.",
  "afcat-r-coding": "1. Sub-topics: Letter Coding (positional shift +n/-n), Number Coding (letter positions summed), Substitution Coding (chain replacement), Message Coding (common word identification across sentences). 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, CDS (OTA). 4. Key Concepts: Intersection method for message coding; chain tracing for substitution; verify code rule with multiple examples before applying.",
  "afcat-r-directions": "1. Sub-topics: Finding final direction, calculating shortest displacement, shadow direction at sunrise/sunset, combined direction-and-distance problems. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, CDS (OTA). 4. Key Concepts: Pythagoras theorem for displacement; shadow at sunrise falls West; shadow at sunset falls East; always draw a diagram.",
  "afcat-r-clock-calendar": "1. Sub-topics: Angle between clock hands (formula: |30h - (11/2)m|), coincidence and perpendicularity of hands, odd days method for calendar, leap year rules including century years. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: 11 coincidences in 12 hours; 22 right-angles in 12 hours; century years divisible by 400 are leap years; odd day codes 0=Sunday to 6=Saturday.",
  "afcat-r-venn": "1. Sub-topics: 10 standard Venn Diagram cases for three categories (nested, disjoint, partially overlapping in all combinations), Venn Diagram analysis questions with numerical data in overlapping regions. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT (3-5 questions, high frequency). 4. Key Concepts: Identifying subset vs. intersection vs. disjoint relationship for each pair of categories before selecting diagram type.",
  "afcat-r-syllogism": "1. Sub-topics: Four standard propositions (A: Universal Affirmative, E: Universal Negative, I: Particular Affirmative, O: Particular Negative), drawing minimum-possibility Venn diagrams, testing each conclusion against all valid diagrams. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, CDS (OTA). 4. Key Concepts: 'Some' claim is weakest; 'All' conclusion requires two universal premises; Either/Or pair for complementary conclusions.",
  "afcat-r-conclusions": "1. Sub-topics: Testing whether conclusions follow necessarily from given statements, identifying invalid conclusions that use absolute language not present in the statement, distinguishing inference from restatement. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, CDS (OTA). 4. Key Concepts: No external knowledge import; absolute words (all/never/always) invalidate most conclusions; conclusion must be a necessary deduction.",
  "afcat-r-assumptions": "1. Sub-topics: Identifying implicit assumptions (necessary unstated premises), testing assumptions using the negation test, distinguishing between stated facts and unstated premises. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT, CDS (OTA). 4. Key Concepts: Negation test — if assumption is false, statement becomes meaningless; absolute words (all/each/every) in assumption usually indicate NOT implicit.",
  "afcat-r-fig-analogy": "1. Sub-topics: Rotation (45/90/135/180 degrees CW or ACW), Reflection (horizontal/vertical), Element Addition/Removal, Size Change, Shading Shift, Element Shift, Replacement. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT (3-4 questions, high frequency). 4. Key Concepts: Component Tracking method — isolate one element at a time to identify the transformation rule before applying it to the third figure.",
  "afcat-r-fig-class-series": "1. Sub-topics: Figure Classification (number of sides, symmetry axis, rotation vs. mirror, arrow direction, shading ratio), Figure Series (rotation pattern, element movement per step, addition/subtraction, alternating patterns). 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT (5-8 combined questions). 4. Key Concepts: Compare all four figures before choosing the odd one; track only ONE component across all frames of a series.",
  "afcat-r-fig-completion": "1. Sub-topics: Axial symmetry (mirror along horizontal/vertical axis), Rotational symmetry (90-degree rotation), Central symmetry (opposite quadrants are 180-degree rotations), Tile/Repetition pattern. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT (3-5 questions, high frequency). 4. Key Concepts: Process of elimination using one specific element in adjacent quadrant; opposite quadrant = 180-degree rotation.",
  "afcat-r-embedded": "1. Sub-topics: Identifying a simple target shape hidden within a complex cluttered figure; orientation rule (target must appear in original orientation, no rotation). 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT (2-4 questions). 4. Key Concepts: Focus on the unique junction, corner, or curve of the target; mentally un-draw extraneous lines; trace the exact outline to confirm.",
  "afcat-r-dot": "1. Sub-topics: Identifying the region where a dot is placed by specifying which shapes it is inside and outside; finding the answer option that has a region satisfying exactly the same conditions. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT (3-4 questions). 4. Key Concepts: Write the condition as In(A) AND In(B) AND Out(C) before scanning options; eliminate options where the required region does not physically exist.",
  "afcat-r-cube-dice": "1. Sub-topics: Painted cube formulas (3-face = 8 corners always; 2-face = 12(n-2); 1-face = 6(n-2)^2; 0-face = (n-2)^3); Standard dice (opposite faces sum to 7: pairs 1-6, 2-5, 3-4); Finding opposite faces from given views using common-face comparison method. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT. 4. Key Concepts: n = number of divisions per edge; standard dice vs general dice distinction.",
  "afcat-r-fig-coding": "1. Sub-topics: Each 2-letter code encodes two visual properties (shape, shading, size, orientation); decoding by grouping figures sharing each code letter to identify the common property; building a decoding table before applying to the unknown figure. 2. Standard: Competitive Aptitude (Class 10th level). 3. Exams: AFCAT (older papers). 4. Key Concepts: Start with the most frequent letter; systematically eliminate options; the coding system is always internally consistent."
};
